    "route": "/countries/tr/visa/work",
    "text": "Turkey - Work Visa. Status: Visa required before travel for Tunisian passport holders. Duration: Contract duration (typically 1–2 years). Entries: Multiple. Fee: Varies — check the official source. Processing time: Varies by permit type — check the official source. Application method: Online/paper application + embassy appointment & biometrics. Notes: A long-stay visa tied to an employment contract. Most countries require the employer to file a permit first.. Required documents: Passport: A valid passport or travel document. Must be valid for at least 3–6 months beyond your intended stay and contain at least two blank pages. Copies of previous passports help too. Visa application form: The completed online or paper visa application form. Printed, dated and signed. Any error can delay the application — review it carefully before submitting. Passport photos: Recent biometric photos that match the destination’s requirements. Typically taken within the last 6 months, on a plain white background, matching the size and format of the destination country (e.g. 35×45 mm for Schengen). Proof of financial means: Bank statements or funds showing you can support the trip. Usually 3–6 months of bank statements. Many consulates require a minimum balance per day of stay (e.g. €50–€120/day). Work contract / permit (if applicable): A signed employment contract or approved work permit. For work visas: a local employment contract or an approved work-authorisation issued by the destination’s authorities. Proof of accommodation: Hotel booking, rental agreement or an invitation with housing proof. A confirmed booking covering every night of the stay, or a signed invitation letter with proof the host can house you. Proof of employment / studies: Evidence of what you do back home and why you will return. Employment contract, payslips, employer leave letter, or proof of enrolment for students — ties that show you intend to return. Previous passport / travel history (if applicable): Old passports showing your travel history. Consulates often consider Schengen history favourably. Bring previous passports or certified copies. Return flight ticket: Confirmed onward or return flight reservation. Many airlines and border officials ask for proof of onward travel on arrival.. Application steps: 1. Secure admission / offer: Obtain an official acceptance letter, contract or permit from the destination. 2. Prepare documents: Gather the long-stay checklist — translations may be required. 3. Complete the long-stay application: Fill the specific long-stay visa or residence application. 4. Book appointment and biometrics: Schedule at the embassy or visa centre in Tunisia. 5. Attend the appointment: Bring originals and copies; an interview may be required. 6. Wait and collect: Processing can take weeks or months — track and collect your visa. Official source: Turkish Ministry of Foreign Affairs / Embassy in Tunis.  Last verified: 2026-11-14.",
