    "route": "/countries/ma/visa/tourism",
    "text": "Morocco - Tourist Visa. Status: Visa-free for Tunisian passport holders. Duration: Short stay — up to 90 days. Entries: Single or Multiple. Fee: None. Processing time: No visa required. Application method: No visa required — present passport on arrival. Notes: A short-stay visa for holidays and sightseeing. You generally cannot work or study while on this visa.. Required documents: Passport: A valid passport or travel document. Must be valid for at least 3–6 months beyond your intended stay and contain at least two blank pages. Copies of previous passports help too. Visa application form: The completed online or paper visa application form. Printed, dated and signed. Any error can delay the application — review it carefully before submitting. Passport photos: Recent biometric photos that match the destination’s requirements. Typically taken within the last 6 months, on a plain white background, matching the size and format of the destination country (e.g. 35×45 mm for Schengen). Travel insurance: Proof of travel medical insurance covering your whole trip. Schengen applications require at least €30,000 in medical cover across the entire Schengen area for the full stay. Proof of accommodation: Hotel booking, rental agreement or an invitation with housing proof. A confirmed booking covering every night of the stay, or a signed invitation letter with proof the host can house you. Proof of financial means: Bank statements or funds showing you can support the trip. Usually 3–6 months of bank statements. Many consulates require a minimum balance per day of stay (e.g. €50–€120/day). Flight / travel information: Round-trip flight reservations and an outline of your trip. Confirmed or reserved return tickets plus a rough day-by-day itinerary. Do not buy non-refundable tickets before approval. Proof of employment / studies: Evidence of what you do back home and why you will return. Employment contract, payslips, employer leave letter, or proof of enrolment for students — ties that show you intend to return. Return flight ticket: Confirmed onward or return flight reservation. Many airlines and border officials ask for proof of onward travel on arrival.. Application steps: 1. Confirm passport validity: Your passport must be valid for your entire stay (check the entry rule for your destination). 2. Prepare entry documents: Have your return ticket, accommodation booking and proof of funds ready to show if asked. 3. Fly to your destination: No visa is required — present your Tunisian passport at immigration. 4. Show documents on arrival: Border officers may ask for proof of accommodation and onward travel. 5. Receive your entry stamp: Stay within the maximum allowed period printed on your entry stamp. 6. Enjoy your stay: Respect local laws and exit before the allowed period ends to avoid overstaying. Official source: Moroccan Ministry of Foreign Affairs.  Last verified: 2026-11-14.",
