    "text": "Egypt - Residence Permit. Status: Visa required before travel for Tunisian passport holders. Duration: 1–5 years, renewable. Entries: Multiple. Fee: Varies — check the official source. Processing time: Varies by permit type — check the official source. Application method: Online/paper application + embassy appointment & biometrics. Notes: For long-term settlement. Requirements differ strongly by country and by reason (work, family, retirement).. Required documents: Passport: A valid passport or travel document. Must be valid for at least 3–6 months beyond your intended stay and contain at least two blank pages. Copies of previous passports help too. Visa application form: The completed online or paper visa application form. Printed, dated and signed. Any error can delay the application — review it carefully before submitting. Passport photos: Recent biometric photos that match the destination’s requirements. Typically taken within the last 6 months, on a plain white background, matching the size and format of the destination country (e.g. 35×45 mm for Schengen). Proof of financial means: Bank statements or funds showing you can support the trip. Usually 3–6 months of bank statements. Many consulates require a minimum balance per day of stay (e.g. €50–€120/day). Proof of residence (if applicable): Documentation of where you live in Tunisia. A residence certificate, utility bill or rental contract confirming your Tunisian address. Work contract / permit (if applicable): A signed employment contract or approved work permit. For work visas: a local employment contract or an approved work-authorisation issued by the destination’s authorities. Marriage / family certificate (if applicable): Documents proving your family relationship. For family reunification or visiting a spouse: certified marriage, birth certificates or family-book extracts. Previous passport / travel history (if applicable): Old passports showing your travel history. Consulates often consider Schengen history favourably. Bring previous passports or certified copies. Proof of accommodation: Hotel booking, rental agreement or an invitation with housing proof. A confirmed booking covering every night of the stay, or a signed invitation letter with proof the host can house you.. Application steps: 1. Secure admission / offer: Obtain an official acceptance letter, contract or permit from the destination. 2. Prepare documents: Gather the long-stay checklist — translations may be required. 3. Complete the long-stay application: Fill the specific long-stay visa or residence application. 4. Book appointment and biometrics: Schedule at the embassy or visa centre in Tunisia. 5. Attend the appointment: Bring originals and copies; an interview may be required. 6. Wait and collect: Processing can take weeks or months — track and collect your visa. Official source: Egyptian Ministry of Foreign Affairs / Embassy in Tunis. Visa portal: https://cs.mfa.gov.eg/en/TUN/faq. Last verified: 2026-11-14.",
