    "route": "/countries/gr/visa/tourism",
    "text": "Greece - Tourist Visa. Status: Visa required before travel for Tunisian passport holders. Duration: Short stay — up to 90 days. Entries: Single or Multiple. Fee: €90 (~297 TND). Processing time: 15 calendar days (up to 30–60 in individual cases). Application method: Online application + embassy/visa centre appointment. Notes: A short-stay visa for holidays and sightseeing. You generally cannot work or study while on this visa.. Required documents: Passport: A valid passport or travel document. Must be valid for at least 3–6 months beyond your intended stay and contain at least two blank pages. Copies of previous passports help too. Visa application form: The completed online or paper visa application form. Printed, dated and signed. Any error can delay the application — review it carefully before submitting. Passport photos: Recent biometric photos that match the destination’s requirements. Typically taken within the last 6 months, on a plain white background, matching the size and format of the destination country (e.g. 35×45 mm for Schengen). Travel insurance: Proof of travel medical insurance covering your whole trip. Schengen applications require at least €30,000 in medical cover across the entire Schengen area for the full stay. Proof of accommodation: Hotel booking, rental agreement or an invitation with housing proof. A confirmed booking covering every night of the stay, or a signed invitation letter with proof the host can house you. Proof of financial means: Bank statements or funds showing you can support the trip. Usually 3–6 months of bank statements. Many consulates require a minimum balance per day of stay (e.g. €50–€120/day). Flight / travel information: Round-trip flight reservations and an outline of your trip. Confirmed or reserved return tickets plus a rough day-by-day itinerary. Do not buy non-refundable tickets before approval. Proof of employment / studies: Evidence of what you do back home and why you will return. Employment contract, payslips, employer leave letter, or proof of enrolment for students — ties that show you intend to return. Return flight ticket: Confirmed onward or return flight reservation. Many airlines and border officials ask for proof of onward travel on arrival.. Application steps: 1. Check eligibility: Confirm you meet the entry conditions for this visa category. 2. Prepare documents: Gather every document in the checklist below. 3. Complete the application: Fill in the official application form online before your appointment. 4. Book your appointment: Reserve a slot at the embassy or visa application centre. 5. Submit application and biometrics: Attend the appointment, provide fingerprints and pay the fee. 6. Wait for the decision: Track your application; most decisions come within the processing time. Official source: Hellenic Ministry of Foreign Affairs / Embassy in Tunis. Visa portal: https://www.mfa.gr/missionsabroad/en/visas.html?mis=tunisia&mission=tun. Last verified: 2026-11-14.",
